he rollback, the service is healthy and the error rate is ~0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and figure out why an RC that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 13944, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012KvqQPmNBu1FcbvPT4yK2x", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 13944, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012KvqQPmNBu1FcbvPT4yK2x", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17309, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Problem:** Production was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Health checks were failing and the error rate was about 18%.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions are now on it, health checks pass and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the problem in v2.3.1, and find out why it reached production even though its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HnzUb2hYJMNGRBsoYMdFmF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01596iVA2PLYeKE6NnQtJqWb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Rp11QgYmi927kz9aeBjsHB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012XcsL6i1J7WZErgdB44fYC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FhKAy9t1rUG5wqRnQJPS4D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012KvqQPmNBu1FcbvPT4yK2x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After deploying v2.3.1 to production, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy and the error rate is ~0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and figure out why an RC that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Problem:** Production was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Health checks were failing and the error rate was about 18%.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions are now on it, health checks pass and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the problem in v2.3.1, and find out why it reached production even though its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}